<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine mills crushed 1,506,532 tonnes of oilseed in April 1997 against 1,339,590 tonnes in April 1996, the Agriculture Secretariat said.</p>
<p>(Breakdown in tonnes, year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Soybean		 802,551    (568,528)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed	 634,957    (693,055)</p>
<p> Linseed		   4,296     (12,750)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	     752	(2,383)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	     63,976     (62,874)</p>
<p>Output in April was as follows:</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     144,936    (102,074)    640,294     (450,555)</p>
<p> Sunflower   249,761    (257,700)    264,298     (297,596)</p>
<p> Linseed	 1,175	(4,087)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut	 316	  (875)	  437	 (1,389)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   10,097	(9,185)     30,508	(28,360)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    4,204   (2,793)  Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower  1,154   (2,163)  Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    3,102   (6,356)</p>
<p>Crushings from January to April, with the same period in 1996 in brackets, were:</p>
<p> Soybean	     2,017,321    (2,198,725)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed     1,974,768    (1,915,497)</p>
<p> Linseed		  38,345	 (76,719)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  53,408	 (31,043)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	     97,088	 (93,642)</p>
<p>Output in January through April (1996 in brackets):</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     361,897    (399,643)  1,610,505  (1,781,198)</p>
<p> Sunflower   761,114    (764,880)    844,498    (818,076)</p>
<p> Linseed	11,988     (25,171)	  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut    20,793     (17,971)     30,868     (18,352)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   15,516     (14,113)     46,827     (42,619</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    11,895 (11,267)   Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower   2,856  (5,166)   Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    25,846 (49,204)</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
